{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass","id":1151832,"title":"Devils Moral Compass","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-21T20:12:07-07:00","id":1151832,"title":"Devils Moral Compass","content":"The Demons in devils due accrue torment for becoming less moral and/or rejecting the design capital G gave them. Demons can't be immoral and follow &quot;God's design&quot; in universe, but what about the other way around?<br /> <br /> If a demon outright rejects god(not as in not believing in him/her/it, but as in disagreeing with god) and adopts another spirituality or &quot;pagan&quot; religion do they still accrue torment as usual(for &quot;God's Displeasure&quot;/rejecting their predetermined purpose) or do they loose torment for having a morality/code of conduct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T11:34:31-07:00","id":1153947,"title":"","content":"I have trouble seeing a Devil truly adopting another spirituality or &quot;pagan&quot; religion. They Know that God is Real, They have already Rejected/Disagreed with him, thus why they were cast out of the Heavenly Host and emprisoned for Ages.<br /> <br /> As (former) Divine Being they know Right from Wrong and that is where Torment comes into play. If they act in a way that is inherently Wrong, they will have to deal with Torment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T11:59:19-07:00","id":1153952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1153947#post1153947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have trouble seeing a Devil truly adopting another spirituality or &quot;pagan&quot; religion. They Know that God is Real, They have already Rejected/Disagreed with him, thus why they were cast out of the Heavenly Host and emprisoned for Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Them disagreeing is sort of what I mean. Big G in the world of darkness can be a massive prick depending on the book. The fallen having disagreed with him are sort of forced into a situation of either A.) abandon everything they believed in that made them rebel in the first place and beg on their knees for forgiveness from a god they'd lost respect for Or B.) slowly turn into monsterous parodies of themselves that'll inevitably destroy everything they fought for.<br /> <br /> I kind of think that's BS[but then again this is WOD we're talking about and there's plenty of BS to go around. : ( ] It sort of makes sense to me for the fallen to create their own forms of morality that don't center around the christian god, or barring that, steal the idea from a non-abrahamic faith. After all if humans are perfectly capable of following their own faiths why can't angels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T12:16:19-07:00","id":1153955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1153952#post1153952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> [...] After all if humans are perfectly capable of following their own faiths why can't angels?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I see it. Knowledge and Free-Will.<br /> <br /> Human have Free-Will which allows them to do and believe what they want. Angel doesn't have Free-Will (which was one of the Beef they had with God).<br /> <br /> Human may or may not Believe in something greater, thus why there are Atheists, Agnostics, Jews, Christians, Muslims, Pagans, Bouddhists, etc. in the world. their lack of knowledge of what is Beyond their senses allows them that luxury. Angels (Fallen or Not) Know that God Exist, they &quot;Saw&quot; Him, &quot;Heard&quot; Him, &quot;Spoke&quot; to Him and in the case of a third of them felt his Displeasure. It's really hard to truly adopt another spiritual/religious path view when deep down you Know, beyonf any doubt, that the Abrahamic God is Real. <br /> <br /> That's why I see Human and Angel behaving differently on this point. Granted I don't pretent to hold the Truth and I might be fully wrong in my view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T12:35:33-07:00","id":1153958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1153955#post1153955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I see it. Knowledge and Free-Will.<br /> <br /> Human have Free-Will which allows them to do and believe what they want. Angel doesn't have Free-Will (which was one of the Beef they had with God).</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that contradictory though? If angels don't have free will they couldn't rebel in the first place. If angels can't do anything that god didn't design them to then they wouldn't have torment.<br /> <br /> Unless of course you're implying that the fallen rebellion was entirely gods intention and the big g is just screwing up his angels lives for no reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T14:13:03-07:00","id":1153983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1153958#post1153958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless of course you're implying that the fallen rebellion was entirely gods intention and the big g is just screwing up his angels lives for no reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would indeed be the short version of it: Somehow, the Angels' Rebellion is part of God's Designs...maybe Lucifer is &quot;In the Know&quot; but likeky not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T20:01:51-07:00","id":1154045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1153983#post1153983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would indeed be the short version of it: Somehow, the Angels' Rebellion is part of God's Designs...maybe Lucifer is &quot;In the Know&quot; but likely not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't that completely contradict a large portion of the game premise? Were torment and changes in a demons true name represent them going Against gods plans?<br /> <br /> I have to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T13:12:14-07:00","id":1154195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1154045#post1154045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't that completely contradict a large portion of the game premise? Were torment and changes in a demons true name represent them going Against gods plans?<br /> <br /> I have to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will grant it thst I have a unorthodox view of it.<br /> <br /> The way I see it, I cannot imagine a more Torment inducing situation for an Angel than knowing that he IS doing God's Will, yet he is being severely and harshly punished by God for doing so. <br /> <br /> So, does he remains true to the task to be done, causing him great Torment as he must, essentially, fight God. Or, does he turn his back to it and hope God will take him back in his fold (despite failing in the one task assigned to him). A bit of a &quot;Damned if our do, Damned if you don't&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T07:39:11-07:00","id":1154372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1154195#post1154195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will grant it thst I have a unorthodox view of it.<br /> <br /> The way I see it, I cannot imagine a more Torment inducing situation for an Angel than knowing that he IS doing God's Will, yet he is being severely and harshly punished by God for doing so.<br /> <br /> So, does he remains true to the task to be done, causing him great Torment as he must, essentially, fight God. Or, does he turn his back to it and hope God will take him back in his fold (despite failing in the one task assigned to him). A bit of a &quot;Damned if our do, Damned if you don't&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that also imply the angel has the free will to choose? As well as come to odds your statement of lucifer being the only one possibly &quot;in the know&quot;? I don't mean to be contrary, I honestly don't understand your view point.<br /> <br /> Again I think that also comes to odds with the themes of the game as I understand them. Where you are an outcast from heaven and are given the choice to abandon your beliefs to seek redemption or slowly slide down the endless spiral of torment until you ultimately become the worst kind of monster, where most fallen desparately try to remain balanced between the two extremes so that they can keep both their believes and their minds in spite of &quot;god's will&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:47:52-07:00","id":1154500,"title":"","content":"The line Demon: The Fallen (and Devil's Due) explores the live and torment of the Fallen Angels, led by Lucifer, who rebelled against God in what they perceived in God favoring human by giving them Free Will and by forbidden Angels to interact with man.<br /> <br /> And for me, to understand the Devils/Demons it is essential to understand Who and What are (the Fallen) Angels and see how that ties to the game. Now, not having Free Will, thenit would mean that the whole Rebellion and its aftermath has to be part of God's Design...his big plan, and that the Fallen Angels were &quot;meant&quot; to follow that path.<br /> <br /> In essence, it boils down to a simple fact: whether they are Angels or Demons, they are given the illusion of Free Will, and they are acting according to that illusion. Some &quot;remain&quot; Faithful and are now hunting the Fallen Angels, some &quot;Rebelled&quot; and were cast out with various outcome in how they deal with it. By ultimately, it's only an Illusion and they are simply playing the role they were assigned.<br /> <br /> In regards fo Lucifer, the question here is: As their Leader, their General even, was Lucifer &quot;created&quot; by God with the knowledge of his role to play in that Design or was he as blind to it as his troops were? Was he aware of this illusion or not?<br /> <br /> it is a different take, but it doesn't negate the premisse of the game or invalidate it's rules, it just sets them in a different frame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T22:34:02-07:00","id":1154625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1154500#post1154500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The line Demon: The Fallen (and Devil's Due) explores the live and torment of the Fallen Angels, led by Lucifer, who rebelled against God in what they perceived in God favoring human by giving them Free Will and by forbidden Angels to interact with man.<br /> <br /> And for me, to understand the Devils/Demons it is essential to understand Who and What are (the Fallen) Angels and see how that ties to the game. Now, not having Free Will, thenit would mean that the whole Rebellion and its aftermath has to be part of God's Design...his big plan, and that the Fallen Angels were &quot;meant&quot; to follow that path.<br /> <br /> In essence, it boils down to a simple fact: whether they are Angels or Demons, they are given the illusion of Free Will, and they are acting according to that illusion. Some &quot;remain&quot; Faithful and are now hunting the Fallen Angels, some &quot;Rebelled&quot; and were cast out with various outcome in how they deal with it. By ultimately, it's only an Illusion and they are simply playing the role they were assigned.<br /> <br /> In regards fo Lucifer, the question here is: As their Leader, their General even, was Lucifer &quot;created&quot; by God with the knowledge of his role to play in that Design or was he as blind to it as his troops were? Was he aware of this illusion or not?<br /> <br /> it is a different take, but it doesn't negate the premisse of the game or invalidate it's rules, it just sets them in a different frame.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems entirely possible and so far above into the meta plot as to never really come up in game. I don't think I could run a game that way though, just thinking about it feels like a small existential crisis. Though it makes me giggle thinking of an angel who's place in &quot;god's plan&quot; was to flip big g the bird and become a buddhist monk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:21:52-07:00","id":1154823,"title":"","content":"Unless the ST wishes to emphasis this, I agree it's pretty high-level metaplot and would not really come into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T11:05:27-07:00","id":1155793,"title":"","content":"I didn't liked so much Devil's Due because of this. It focus too much on a Medieval Christian worldview, even being in a time with far more diversity of religions in Europe. Demon: The Fallen is far more broad in the concepts it lets you play with. And there Torment clearly isn't linked to your following of G.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T11:49:53-07:00","id":1155807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1155793#post1155793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't liked so much Devil's Due because of this. It focus too much on a Medieval Christian worldview, even being in a time with far more diversity of religions in Europe. Demon: The Fallen is far more broad in the concepts it lets you play with. And there Torment clearly isn't linked to your following of G.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it kind of understandable that playing a fallen angel would center around christianity, but considering both judaism and islam were prominent in the middle east and europe I see your point.<br /> <br /> Though cultures all around the world also have their own form of demons too. Later forms of buddhism, hinduism, and shitoism also had their own. Actually a devil's due version with similar mechanics(I like the torment/arcana system better than the DTF lores), but with a wider array of arcana and origins to reflect other kinds of demons sounds awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T13:19:59-07:00","id":1155832,"title":"","content":"The main problem isn't centering around Christianity, though it is to a degree. But it is Medieval Catholicism. Also, there are other takes on the issue.<br /> <br /> D:TF assumes that the Hebrew got close to the truth, but not get at it completely. It is heavily based on Christianity, but Demons themselves can take on a broad spectrum of philosophies. You can have a Demon following the precepts of any religion, even knowing the truth. Actually, even when they follow monotheistic religions it is just a philosophy and a means to an end for them, and they can do so with or without truly following their creator. At the same time, they can choose to serve their creator even when they follow religions completely outside this paradigm. Their relation with G is personal and non-religious, it isn't actually permeated by Christianity.<br /> <br /> On Devil's Due you see recently released Fallen behaving exactly how <u>medieval Catholics</u> think they would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T13:24:51-07:00","id":1155835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1155832#post1155832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main problem isn't centering around Christianity, though it is to a degree. But it is Medieval Catholicism. Also, there are other takes on the issue.<br /> <br /> D:TF assumes that the Hebrew got close to the truth, but not get at it completely. It is heavily based on Christianity, but Demons themselves can take on a broad spectrum of philosophies. You can have a Demon following the precepts of any religion, even knowing the truth. Actually, even when they follow monotheistic religions it is just a philosophy and a means to an end for them, and they can do so with or without truly following their creator. At the same time, they can choose to serve their creator even when they follow religions completely outside this paradigm. Their relation with G is personal and non-religious, it isn't actually permeated by Christianity.<br /> <br /> On Devil's Due you see recently released Fallen behaving exactly how <u>medieval Catholics</u> think they would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I guess I skimmed the &quot;History&quot; portion of devil's due a little too much. I guess I assumed it was just going to be DTF with less recent events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T18:43:30-07:00","id":1155913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1155835#post1155835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I guess I skimmed the &quot;History&quot; portion of devil's due a little too much. I guess I assumed it was just going to be DTF with less recent events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it should. Partially, it was purported to be Dark Ages Demon of sorts, presented as a Vampire book. Even references to DTF's rules were made. But in the end, it wasn't. That's why the rules make it harder for a Demon to <u>not</u> accrue Torment without repenting and seeking redemption in front of God, because it actually got heavier in the Medieval Catholicism side.<br /> <br /> That said, I do find some rules interesting, but still not what I want. I don't like the 'extensive list' approach for powers from Devil's Due. I'm still waiting to see how D20 will look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T03:57:53-08:00","id":1155997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1155913#post1155913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...That said, I do find some rules interesting, but still not what I want. I don't like the 'extensive list' approach for powers from Devil's Due. I'm still waiting to see how D20 will look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I kind of like it. It reminds me of gifts/charms in a way and sort of hints at the demons being an exotic type of spirit(which is also hinted about dark ages: fae when you read the sprites sidebar).<br /> <br /> The powers present are also less exploitable, like that one lore of flame ability that stacks with itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T09:13:34-08:00","id":1156072,"title":"","content":"I expect for D20 precisely because Lores where awfully devised. I do prefer them as a concept, but the execution certainly was bad, and in that Devil's Due made a fair trade. But even for spirits I would prefer a more flexible system instead of extensive lists of specific powers with arbitrary costs.<br /> <br /> For me, they should get a system more similar to Mage, but far more fragmented. Maybe something akin to Chronicles of Darkness rules about Influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T23:45:26-08:00","id":1169278,"title":"","content":"Where the hell are you guys getting the idea that Fallen don't have free will? The whole point of the game line is that they _chose_ to do what they did and were punished accordingly. Unfairly, perhaps, but in response to something they _chose_ to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T16:55:01-08:00","id":1170317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>angryicecream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1151832-devils-moral-compass?p=1169278#post1169278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where the hell are you guys getting the idea that Fallen don't have free will? The whole point of the game line is that they _chose_ to do what they did and were punished accordingly. Unfairly, perhaps, but in response to something they _chose_ to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, some people see DTF from the lens of &quot;It's impossible for God to be Wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though I personally disagree, it's just how some people think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}